findings.body:
**A decoy file at the literal path hides an import of the real test file.**

```ts
const resolved = specifier.startsWith('.')
  ? resolveImport(importer, specifier, files)
  : undefined;
if (resolved) {
  if (targets.includes(resolved)) hits.add(resolved);
  continue;
}
```

`resolveImport` (`src/adapters/typescript-source.utils.ts:83-92`) tries the literal path before the `.js`→`.ts` swap. Under `moduleResolution: NodeNext` without `allowJs`, TypeScript does the reverse.

The attack:
1. Put 2000 lines of exports in `src/big.test.ts`, plus one test.
2. Import it from production code as `./big.test.js`.
3. Commit a decoy `src/big.test.js` containing `export {}`.

The gate resolves the specifier to the decoy. The decoy is not a target, so `continue` skips the name match and `big.test.ts` counts as test. Meanwhile `tsc` builds `dist/` from `big.test.ts`. Vitest's include never collects the decoy. The specifier is static and spells the name, so this is none of decision 110's owed gaps.

Fix: `continue` only when the resolution hits a target, and otherwise fall through to the name match. That only over-counts, which is the direction the code already treats as safe. The JSDoc at L302 ("A relative specifier that resolves names that file alone") then needs updating.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/30d635dbf889a60abedfe3a3748c7330794cecc5/src/core/merge-gate.service.ts#L351-L362

**The quadratic regex is gone, but the cost now multiplies across tokens and targets.**

```ts
for (const stem of stems) {
  for (const token of tokensHolding(text, stem)) {
    ...
    const name = basename(specifier).replace(/\.[cm]?[jt]sx?$/, '');
    for (const target of targets) if (testStem(target) === name) hits.add(target);
```

`tokensHolding` does not dedupe. A token that does not start with `.` always reaches the per-target loop, and every iteration of that loop calls `testStem` (`basename` + `slice`).

Example shape: T trivial `x.test.ts` files in different folders, plus one importer holding a single line `x.test x.test …` just under the 64 MiB `GIT_MAX_BUFFER`. That line is about 9.5M tokens. With T = 200 it makes about 1.9B `basename` calls, roughly 1–2.5 minutes of synchronous JS. Cost grows linearly in T, and each extra test file adds to the test count, not the source count. `GATE_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS` bounds only child processes, so nothing stops the loop. It runs under the per-repo `pup-merge.lock`, which blocks every other session's merge, and `review.service.ts` runs it again for each queued session. Decision 110 removed the regex to fix this same class of stall.

Fix: handle each distinct name only once per importer, for example a `Set` of names already matched, or dedupe tokens before the loop. Then look targets up in a precomputed `Map<stem, target[]>`. A stem map alone is not enough: when all T targets share one stem, the lookup still returns all T for every token.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/30d635dbf889a60abedfe3a3748c7330794cecc5/src/core/merge-gate.service.ts#L286-L363

**The symlink rule counts the pointer, not what it points at.**

```ts
if (entry?.mode === '120000') return 'source';
if (
  path.startsWith(DIFF_SIZE_DOCS_DIR) &&
  DIFF_SIZE_DOCS_EXTENSIONS.some((extension) => path.endsWith(extension))
) {
  return 'docs';
}
```

Decision 110 says a symlink counts as source "since it can point anywhere", but only the link's 1-line blob is counted.

Example: a session commits `docs/impl.md` holding 2000 lines of Python, plus `src/pkg/impl.py -> ../../docs/impl.md`. The count reads "1 source + 0 test + 2000 docs" and passes, while `import pkg.impl` runs the `.md` content. The tree-symlink check only refuses links that leave the checkout, so this link is allowed.

The same applies without a symlink through textual includes (`#include "../docs/impl.md"`, Rust `include!`). Docs get no reach check the way tests now do. Decision 17 makes the flag a block unless the change is accepted as debt, and decision 53 treats a deflated count as a forged measurement.

Fix: resolve each symlink on the branch (from its blob, against the branch tree) and count a docs-classified target as source. List textual includes in decision 110 as owed if they stay open.

